From: mscharged-port
Subject: Rollback: the sounds with a context follow the match as well
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

Patch 0046 has the tracked sounds follow the match. The other sounds
started with a context (PlaySound, PlayOwnedSound), which StopSound finds
again by cue and context, had the same fault: a loop that only a replay
stopped played on, as Bowser's, Wario's and Waluigi's super abilities'
(TankOn) or a powerup's while it flies; and a sound that only a replay
started was lost, as the dazed stars or a slide attack's. With predicted
inputs that is every such sound the other player's late input brings.

They now join the same tables, the entry noting whether the sound is
tracked (only those pause and resume) and the owner that places it (the
ball's, which lives through the match). The reconciliation starts them
again with PlayOwnedSound, from the start, as late as the rollback found
them. PlayTrackedSound's own start through PlaySound counts once. The
crowd's reactions (PlayCrowdReaction, StopCrowdReactions) stay out: no
replay runs them, so a rollback taking one back from the table would end
it. The tables hold 64 sounds.

A sound started again after a rollback has none of the parameters its
start set afterwards (SetLastSoundParameter). The one-shot sounds without
a context are left as they are.

